   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to the appointment of\nmembers of the public service commission",
    "basePrintNo": "S7145",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7145-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7145\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to the appointment\nof members of the public service commission\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo improve oversight of utilities by setting clearly defined statutory\nqualifications for prospective members of the Public Service Commission\n(PSC).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 4 of the public service law by\nadding a new subdivision 4, which provides that any person appointed on\nor after July 1, 2020 as a PSC commissioner shall (a) have education and\ntraining and 3 or more years of experience in one or more of the follow-\ning fields: economics, engineering, law, accounting, business manage-\nment, utility regulation, public policy, consumer advocacy or environ-\nmental management;\n\nSection 2 of the bill sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAfter a massive power outage hit Queens, the Assembly Queens Power\nOutage Task Force was established to study the outage's causes. The Task\nForce recommended that, unlike many other states, New York does not have\nany substantive statutory standards for who may serve on the PSC. This\nbill sets forth such standards to require relevant education and train-\ning of PSC commissioners that are appointed after July 1, 2020\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: A3819 (Rozic) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2019: A3819 (Rozic) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2018: A9697 (Rozic) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2017: A08608 (Kavanagh)- Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2016: A05771 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2015: A05771 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2014: A00177 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2013: A00177 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2012: A01643 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2011: A01643 (Kavanagh) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2010: A01671 (Gianaris) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2009: A01671 (Gianaris) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2008: A08619 (Gianaris) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n2007: A08619 (Gianaris) - Corporations, Authorities & Commissions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred twentieth day after it\nshall have become a law.\n",
